      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_50",
        on: "choice",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:clear_shroud",
            side: 1,
            xs: 22,
            ys: 9,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:lift_fog",
            side: 1,
            cells: "22,9",
            radius: 2,
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Afalas",
            text: _("I see torches movin’ in the fog... Thank th’ light, it’s living men!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Afalas",
            text: _("Please, please, just hear me out. I knows my men and I’ve done evil, and I knows that you seek to destroy us out of revenge. Ah’m sorry my brothers attacked you. It was never my intention to cause everyone so much suffering."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Ethiliel",
            portrait: "portraits/ethiliel-mad.webp",
            text: _("It was “never your intention”!? You loathsome vermin locked me in a cage! You dragged Mebrin off in chains; my kind, gentle teacher! Deoran, why are we stooping so low as to even speak with this pig?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Afalas",
            text: _("I swear I ain’t your enemy! I’ll gladly tell ye what I know. I admit that near a year ago, me brothers and I ventured into the valley of the elves in secret, to plunder and steal. Many we killed. It was wrong, I know, and I am sorry for it."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Afalas",
            text: _("But there was one who we captured; a powerful and magical sage. Away from his people, he offered to teach us the secrets o’ summonin’ the dead. I saw the folly in doing such a thing, but my brothers were weak an’ foolish, and soon fell under the sway of the corrupting magic — becomin’ thralls of the very elf they’d sought to enslave. They called him “master”, and went from here to do his bidding."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Ethiliel",
            portrait: "portraits/ethiliel-mad.webp",
            text: _("A complete and utter lie from complete and utter scum. I studied magic under Mebrin for many decades and know him well — my teacher would never lead undead, he would destroy them!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Afalas",
            text: _("It’s true that Mebrin was more powerful than any of the corpses we raised, yet he didn’t resist ’em. They took him into the caves, and soon after skeletal horrors started to emerge."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Afalas",
            text: _("Now my boys and I have returned to try an’ put a stop to it, but there’s just too many. Unless ye helps me now, Mebrin’s undead may soon be strong enough to besiege Westin itself!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Afalas",
            text: _("I knows I’m a criminal. My men and I have committed wrongdoing’s in the past, but at least in the fight against the undead, we can be your friends! They’re as much our enemies as they’re yours!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Ethiliel",
            text: _("Deoran, you would trust the word of a thief and murderer over me, your friend and ally? This criminal will abandon you the moment he finds a chance!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Ethiliel",
            text: _("Think of the destruction this man and his brothers wrought on your people. Think of the horrors they inflicted upon me, caged and left to suffer amidst the stinking corpses of my friends! Believe the truths you have seen, not the lies you have heard. No fake niceties can reverse the deaths that have already happened; no atonement taken now can set right the transgressions that have already come to pass!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "dialogue",
            children: [
              {
                tag: "message",
                speaker: "Deoran",
                text: _("Peace, let me think! <i>If I listen to Ethiliel I must fight the bandits, but if I ally with the bandits Ethiliel will surely abandon us...</i>"),
              },
              {
                tag: "choice",
                text: _("Side with Ethiliel"),
                event: "ev_50_opt0",
              },
              {
                tag: "choice",
                text: _("Side with Afalas"),
                event: "ev_50_opt1",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:modify_turns",
            value: 30,
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "if_52",
